{
  "about": "The board-reference language (.kicad_pcb), asserted by packages/core/src/lib/boardRefs.js and cad/engine/formats/kicad/refs.py alike. A part is its reference designator (a letter or '_', then letters, digits, '_', '+' or '-': what KiCad boards and board.part(ref=...) use), a pad follows a dot, a net is net:<name> (JSON-quoted when the name holds whitespace, a quote, a comma, '@' or '#'), and a point is @x<x>y<y> in KiCad's millimetres (y down, from the page origin): comma-free, because a token joins several selectors with commas, as STEP tokens do (split outside quotes); whitespace inside a quoted name is the name's, anywhere else it ends the token. An item (a track, a via, a zone, a text, a dimension, a graphic shape) is <kind>:<uuid>, the uuid KiCad saved it with, lower case in the canonical form; one of the copies of a footprint that share their items' uuids is <kind>:<footprint uuid>/<uuid>. A point may name a layer before its @ (F.Cu@x1y2: KiCad's own layer names); an area is two corners joined by .. (@x1y2..x3y4), its canonical form low corner first. Canonical points drop trailing zeros and a negative zero.",
